A||N||6||BlackARROW||Backup light switch, Super & Naphta||||5||
Z||000000||BlackARROW||04-24-2001||10:36 PM||||My backup lights stopped working a while ago.  Since I've got a 5%-light teinted window in the back, I wish I could see something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Well I tried to change the bulbs, but they were ok. I got no power on my test light, neither at the blue wire (connector below the hose).  My book here says that it must be the backup light switch.  I followed the wire 'til that lil thing there.  Ever played with that?  Or ever experienced the same problem?<P>Another lil concern here, I got a small problem: a coolant fine leak at running near the water pump. Since I changed it not so long ago, I'm sure it's the clamps holding that good old hoses I've gotta change.  I was tired of buying and putting coolant in (50%water), since it was going to leak of the road (drop by drop).  I saw a label in the trunk earlier today, saying to put special coolant.  I was just wondering what they were talking about.<P>I put only Super in for gas, I saw somewhere on the web that it would be best to adjust the timing of some degrees. First, do you prefer putting Super?  Some people tell me it makes no difference, but I think my Super (even for an old '85) is more effecient.<P>Ever heard about Naphtaline Balls as a Add-in supply in the gas?  Just wondered who knew, and who tried, before risking to blow my motor.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good ride to you all.. summer's gonna be great<P>BlackARROW<BR>Fiero 2M4 '85||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||04-25-2001||05:02 PM||||OK, I can help you with the first two.<P>Your first question. What Trans. do you have? It must be the backup light switch.<P>Question 2 That just means that Fieros must have the coolant filled from the back thermostat cap. If you fill from the radiator it will leave a huge air pocket in the cooling system because the radiator is lower than the engine.<P>Hope this helps and welcome to the forum.<P><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000002||Spektyr||04-25-2001||07:30 PM||||Dunno what the Naptha is, but it sounds a lot like a trick a guy I knew in the Navy used to do with mothballs.  Do NOT do that with a motor you want to drive more than a mile.<P>This guy would go out to a junkyard and find a VW bug that ran.  Didn't make any difference if it ran well, had seats, tires, body panels, etc.  Just that it ran.  He'd buy enough parts to make it driveable, and then tow it out to the track.<P>When no one was looking he'd drop 4-5 mothballs in the tank, pull up to the line, and blow the doors off a supercharged Camaro, Mustang, whatever.  Of course EVERYONE wanted to know what he was running, but he wouldn't let them see.  After the second run (and second win) he'd charge $50 a person to look under the hood, which of course revealed a bone stock Bug motor.<P>Third run blew the motor.  Mothballs are mostly ether...<P>Dunno if that's what you're talking about, but if they're even related it's more likely to blow the motor than anything else.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackARROW||04-25-2001||08:06 PM||||Thanks.  I'll keep putting water until I tight the hose with new clamps.<P>I have a 5-speed manual transmission.  I think it's the backup switch too.  I just can't see it properly (good old car)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Can I just pull on it or how can I change that thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I want to see when I back up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks F64<P>BlackARROW<BR>Fiero 2M4 '85<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||BlackARROW||04-25-2001||08:15 PM||||Spektyr, you're right.  I was talking about mothballs (I didn't know how to say that in english)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Well these balls are usually made with 99.83% Naphthalene (which is very volatile).  I heard about the effect it could have on motors, but not as much as you describe me.  Maybe you're buddy put too much?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe  even that, 4 or 5 tells you how powerful and damageable it could be for your motor.  If one day my motor is dying, I'll surely give it a try to feel some Gz at last with that IronDuke.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>Have fun! <BR>Blue skies!<P>BlackARROW<BR>Fiero 2M4 '85  <BR>(I shall put a picture of it in further reply)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spektyr||04-25-2001||10:13 PM||||Well, yeah he used WAY too much... I mean you're talking about beating a blown motor with a Bug.  The object wasn't to make it to the finals, he made his cash charging people to look under the hood.  If I'm not mistaken, Napthalene is the same thing as Ether, and I know Ether detonates at 6:1 compression.  So even very small amounts of Ether in the fuel/air mixture creates BIG time detonation.<P>However, the problem is that it's VERY tricky.  You put a solid into the gas tank (the mothballs) and they dissolve into the gas.  You won't know if it's too much until they've dissolved, at which point you discover this when the motor goes 'Kibbles and Bits' on you.  Or there's always the chance that a tiny solid particle gets into the fuel line where it dissolves making a sudden high-concentration area of fuel.  If that hits on a shift, the motor will redline.  If you run just a tad bit too much, the motor will not idle, the fuel will be so volatile it detonates and the motor will rev to redline and blow itself sky high.<P>You pretty much have two options if you want to affect the volatility of your air/fuel mixture.  Nitrous or nitrous.  I guess you could also use nitrous.  Anything else and you're just asking to have your motor become a very large, very expensive and very impracticle paperweight.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?<p>[This message has been edited by Spektyr (edited 04-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||BlackARROW||04-26-2001||01:04 AM||||I've done some research for us.  They are both biocatalysis.<P>Naphthalene is a bicyclic HydroCarbone<BR>It's formula is C10 H8<BR>Synonym: white tar, mothballs<P>Ethyl acetate's formula is C4 H8 O2<BR>Synonym: ether, acetic acid, vinegar naphtha<P>We were not so far  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>#source: <A HREF="http://umbbd.ahc.umn.edu:8007" TARGET=_blank>http://umbbd.ahc.umn.edu:8007</A> <P>||||reg||1
